# HUD Stability

For `ui/stats_popout.py` and HUD-related UI work:

- Keep resize behavior deterministic and non-blocking.
- Never allow stuck interactive resize state; always provide cleanup/failsafe.
- Avoid re-entrant layout loops; debounce expensive reflow work.
- Do not trigger heavy relayout on every mouse-move while dragging.
- Prevent launch-state glitches (stale scroll position, misaligned content origin).
- Keep compact settings stable after mouse release (no rubber-band relayout surprises).
- Preserve user choices for scale/columns/subtitle visibility across restarts.

Before finishing HUD work:
- Stress test edge/corner resizing
- Verify no cursor lockups
- Verify no clipping in compact mode
